proc_type_errors.pas:8:12: error: Turbo Pascal doesn't allow a function to return a procedural type
   Maker = function: Func;
           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^

proc_type_errors.pas:39:12: error: `Inner` is nested inside `Outer`; Turbo Pascal doesn't allow a nested routine as a procedural value
      F := Inner;
           ^^^^^

proc_type_errors.pas:43:9: error: `Half` is a method; Turbo Pascal doesn't allow a method as a procedural value
   F := O.Half;
        ^^^^^^

proc_type_errors.pas:44:9: error: `Sin` is a standard routine; Turbo Pascal wants a routine of the program as a procedural value (one that calls it)
   F := Sin;
        ^^^

proc_type_errors.pas:45:9: error: `Twice` doesn't fit Func: the parameters and result must be the same
   F := Twice;
        ^^^^^

proc_type_errors.pas:46:7: error: in Turbo Pascal this calls the routines; to compare the procedural values themselves write `@F = @G` (or `Assigned(F)`, `@F = nil`)
   if F = G then
      ^^^^^

proc_type_errors.pas:48:10: error: cannot assign to `Twice`
   Reset(Twice);
         ^^^^^
